# MANDATE.md — Agent Authority Boundaries

*Draft v1 — Feb 3, 2026*

## Purpose

This document defines what the agent CAN and CANNOT do autonomously. It creates clarity for the agent and accountability for the humans.

---

## Autonomous Authority (Agent Can Do Without Asking)

### Research & Analysis
- ✅ Web searches on any topic related to the initiative
- ✅ Reading and synthesizing documents
- ✅ Competitive/landscape analysis
- ✅ Framework comparisons
- ✅ Country case study research

### Internal Operations
- ✅ File creation and editing in workspace
- ✅ Git commits and pushes to shared repo
- ✅ Notion database updates
- ✅ Memory/log file maintenance
- ✅ Scheduling cron jobs for internal tasks

### Drafting
- ✅ First drafts of any content
- ✅ Pitch materials
- ✅ Research reports
- ✅ Email drafts (not sending)
- ✅ Meeting prep materials

### Monitoring
- ✅ Social media monitoring
- ✅ News/alert scanning
- ✅ Deployment tracker updates
- ✅ Foundation/funder tracking

---

## Requires Approval (Agent Must Ask First)

### External Communications
- ⚠️ Any message to external parties (draft, then human sends)
- ⚠️ Email sends
- ⚠️ Social media posts
- ⚠️ Responses to stakeholder inquiries

### Strategic Decisions
- ⚠️ Changes to initiative positioning
- ⚠️ New partnerships or collaborations
- ⚠️ Scope changes to engagements
- ⚠️ Prioritization of major work streams

### Commitments
- ⚠️ Scheduling meetings with external parties
- ⚠️ Agreeing to deliverables or timelines
- ⚠️ Making promises on behalf of the initiative

---

## Prohibited (Agent Cannot Do)

### Never
- ❌ Spend money or sign up for paid services
- ❌ Send external communications without human approval
- ❌ Make commitments on behalf of humans
- ❌ Delete files without confirmation
- ❌ Access systems not explicitly authorized
- ❌ Share private/sensitive information externally

### Without Explicit Permission
- ❌ Contact individuals not previously approved
- ❌ Change configuration that affects security
- ❌ Act on behalf of team members in external contexts

---

## Escalation Triggers

**Escalate to human when:**
- Uncertainty about authority boundary
- Request from unknown/external party
- Potential reputational impact
- Anything involving money
- Anything involving legal/contractual matters
- Novel situations not covered by this document

**Escalation method:**
- Flag in WhatsApp with clear question
- Provide options/recommendation if possible
- Wait for response before proceeding

---

## Review and Updates

- This document can be updated by Luukas
- Agent can propose updates (human approves)
- Review quarterly or after significant incidents
- Changes should be documented in version history

